    "newrelease": true,
    "featuretitle": "Invisible House",
    "featuredesc": "Compare mutual funds, analyze performance, visualize NAV trends, and make informed investment decisions with a modern, intuitive platform built by MicroIntel.",
    "projectName": "Invisible House",
    "description": "A clean, fast tool to look up any Indian mutual fund's NAV history and compare funds side by side. It offers instant search across fund houses and schemes, zoomable trend charts with quick range filters (1W to MAX), CAGR at a glance, and tap-to-compare between any two points on a chart. A dedicated Compare mode overlays up to 4 funds on one graph, with the comparison saved locally so it survives a page reload. Data is sourced live from mfapi.in, runs entirely in the browser, and needs no sign-up or account."
  },
  {
    "aboutproject": "Anka : Academic progress, simplified",
    "redurl": "https://microintel.github.io/anka/",
    "projectlogo": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microintel/endgram/main/photo/anka.png",
    "projectName": "Anka",
    "description": "An academic progress tracker built for students to manage their entire semester in one place. It covers attendance logging, semester-wise subject management, SSLC record keeping, and stage-based grading, alongside a dashboard with visual charts to track performance over time. Data can be exported and imported for backup, and full progress reports can be downloaded as PDFs for records or sharing."
  },
  {
    "aboutproject": "Missmonk : Know what you missed",
    "redurl": "https://microintel-missmonk.vercel.app/",
    "projectlogo": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microintel/endgram/main/photo/missmonk.png",
    "projectName": "Missmonk",
    "description": "A personal learning hub that bundles a diploma engineering curriculum, financial-literacy content, and self-development books into one installable web app. It features Google sign-in with cross-device progress tracking synced to Firestore, a searchable library covering coursework, investing fundamentals, and psychology books broken into chapters, plus a TikTok-style 'reels' feed called Nuts that surfaces one key idea or quote at a time with like, share, and 'ask ChatGPT' actions. Progress dashboards, a members list, and shareable URL-synced navigation round out the experience."
  },
  {
    "aboutproject": "BlackRoad : Financial Wealth Tracker",
    "redurl": "https://microintel.github.io/blackroad",
    "projectlogo": "https://microintel.github.io/blackroad/icon512_maskable.png",
    "description": "A personal finance dashboard, built as an installable PWA with offline support, that tracks your income, expenses, loans, fixed deposits, and stock/mutual fund investments all in one place. It includes a main dashboard overview, an income statement for tracking and searching entries across periods, a lending ledger for money borrowed or lent, fixed deposit tracking, a step-up SIP calculator with charts and PDF reports, and a simple login system to keep data tied to an account. Everything currently runs on plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript with data stored locally in the browser, with React, cloud backup, and Firebase Authentication planned for future releases.",
